{"schema":"LAW_EN_DOCUMENT_V1","id":"i18n-7ea716d811e2fdba94a7568a732dea3671cf2ef5210ae6d8","family_id":"KR:013220","country":"KR","language":"en","title":"ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE ACT ON MANAGEMENT OF FIREFIGHTING EQUIPMENT","title_original":"소방장비관리법 시행령","kind":"대통령령","source_version":"287377","promulgated":null,"effective":null,"translation_status":"AI_DRAFT","body_status":"BODY_LOADED","source_url":"https://www.law.go.kr/LSW/lsInfoP.do?lsiSeq=287377","source_sha256":"5ec8ed6d9986beb9b06e27df3fdfd117ffbb23733f907e5568d570449f38d7fc","body_sha256":"2cd6943170ae5c0fbcf8a2703fc86e98c1a7bb77da36dd015bacd36b56a77023","article_count":1,"full_text":"Article 3 (Establishment of Master Plan) (1) The Fire Commissioner of the National Fire Agency shall formulate a master plan by no later than September 30 of the year before the year in which the concerned plan is to be implemented.\n  (2) The Fire Commissioner of the National Fire Agency shall formulate an action plan on management of fire equipment pursuant to Article 4 (3) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as “action plan”) by October 31 of the year before the year in which the concerned plan is to be implemented.\n  (3) The Fire Commissioner of the National Fire Agency shall send the master plan and action plan submitted to the competent standing committee of the National Assembly pursuant to Article 4 (5) of the Act to the heads of the relevant central administrative agencies, the Special Metropolitan City Mayor, the Integrated Special City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayors, the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, Do Governors, the Governor of a Special Self-Governing Province (hereinafter referred to as \"Mayor/Do Governor\"). <Amended on June 23, 2026>","metadata":{"author_checks":["All current held source unit text, source editorial notes, amounts, periods, exceptions and source omission boundaries compared.","Unchanged official English retained only in the recorded exact source/target spans; original row, role, prov